{"name":"Turnip Boy","hex":"#efc6a1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turnip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The white root of a yellow-flowered plant, Brassica rapa, grown as a vegetable and as fodder for cattle.","The yellow root of a related plant, the swede or Brassica napus."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To plant with turnips.","To feed or graze (livestock) on turnips."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turnip"},{"term":"boy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bodo (Central Africa)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A young man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turnip","blocks":[{"text":"The turnip or white turnip is a root vegetable commonly grown in temperate climates worldwide for its white, fleshy taproot. Small, tender varieties are grown for human consumption, while larger varieties are grown as feed for livestock. The name turnip – used in many regions – may also be used to refer to swede, which is a different but related vegetable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Turnip_2622027.jpg/330px-Turnip_2622027.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnip","wikidata":"Q3916957"},{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy","wikidata":"Q3010"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Hakurei_turnips_%2849856034022%29.jpg/500px